From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.mediacontrol: a weak reference, ISystemMediaTransportControls2 and timeline properties (5947)

windows.media.mediacontrol: a weak reference, ISystemMediaTransportControls2 and timeline properties

Spotify crashed at start (a NULL read in Spotify.dll, the SG Store walk:
"no process"). It asks the SystemMediaTransportControls of its window for
IWeakReferenceSource when it adds its ButtonPressed handler (C++/WinRT, as
every Windows runtime object has one), then for
ISystemMediaTransportControls2, and makes a
SystemMediaTransportControlsTimelineProperties for
UpdateTimelineProperties; each was missing and it used the NULL it got.

The control now has a weak reference (resolving to the control while it is
held, to nothing after), ISystemMediaTransportControls2 (AutoRepeatMode,
ShuffleEnabled, PlaybackRate with their defaults, UpdateTimelineProperties,
the four change-requested events), and the timeline properties class is
activatable. qa4: Spotify starts and shows its sign-in. Gate
test-wmc-stubs; mutants SG_MUTANT_SMTC_NO_WEAKREF,
SG_MUTANT_SMTC_NO_CONTROLS2, SG_MUTANT_SMTC_NO_TIMELINE.
